37	// The spec's large-number example: M=math.MaxInt64, window length 7, slide 4
38	// (not a divisor). Events at M-5 (value 2) and M-4 (value 3). Each event is
39	// counted once in every window that contains it, with the full value added;
40	// the second event sits exactly on the right edge of [M-11,M-4) and therefore
41	// enters only the later [M-7,M) window. A watermark strictly below a window
42	// end closes nothing; equality is what emits. An end exactly equal to M is a
43	// legal, representable window end and must not be reported as overflow.
44	func TestAggregateSlidingBigTimeWindowEndAtMaxInt64(t *testing.T) {
